For the probability measure $\mu$ of Theorem <a href="#thm:main" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="thm:main">1</a>, $$\inf_{\substack{T_2,T_3:\mathbb R^3\to\mathbb R^3\ \mathrm{Borel}\\
                 (T_2)_\#\mu=(T_3)_\#\mu=\mu}}
 \int c(x,T_2(x),T_3(x))\,d\mu(x)=E_*(\mu).$$ Every pair in this infimum has cost strictly greater than the common infimum, but pairs with finite cost approach it.
